WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.150
Each of you is to come up with an attraction 
for the cultural festival by Sunday

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:04.150
Abenon, wanna walk home together?

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.100
Huh?

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.100
An attraction for the cultural festival, huh?

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:13.900
Saga and Fusshi, did you 
already pick something?

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:20.200
<b>Cream Puffs</b>

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.620
I'm going with Russian roulette cream puffs.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:20.200
<b>Convenience Store</b>

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.440
I chose a convenience store.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.200
What about you, Abeno-san?

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:22.200
Huh?

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.650
I'm heading out.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.530
Later.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:28.960
Bye.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.710
Ashiya, you're not working today, right?

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:32.350
Yeah.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:35.720
Let's get that new ice cream at the 
convenience store on the way home.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.360
The rich Japanese black 
beef sukiyaki ice cream.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.350
<b>Incoming Call</b>

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.350
Sorry, I'm gonna take this.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.250
Hello?

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.140
Yes...

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.290
Last month's back-fat pork broth 
ramen ice cream was amazing.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.650
Yeah, I was surprised by how good it was.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:56.060
I know. It was so light despite being fatty.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:59.040
Yeah, the texture wasn't 
what I expected, either.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.060
Mononokean, come.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:09.770
There you are!

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.630
Huh?

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.040
I told you I was going 
to the Underworld today.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.510
You have the day off.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:22.520
What's the matter?

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.020
I need a favor.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:31.550
Just now, my mother collapsed at her shop.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:35.000
She's been taken to the hospital.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.920
Could you take me to the hospital?

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:41.980
Go put on your shoes.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.630
Opening a door to Toyama 
Memorial General Hospital.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.400
Thank you.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.720
Toyama Memorial
General Hospital

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.780
<b>Ashiya Nara-sama</b>

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:48.410
<b>Mystery 9 "The Shadow"</b>

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.090
I heard it's anemia?

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.630
I suddenly felt dizzy.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:06.840
They're keeping me here for a day, 
just to be on the safe side.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:12.350
It's been so long. I've been 
healthy since I had you,

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.520
but I used to collapse from anemia 
all the time when I was young.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:20.040
This nostalgic feeling of unwellness 
brings back so many memories.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.370
I'm glad you're doing better than I—

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.210
<i>Fuzzy?!</i>

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.430
My headache is getting worse.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.190
<i>She's anemic because of Fuzzy?!</i>

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.670
<i>No, Fuzzy just got here.</i>

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:44.650
<i>Could it be...</i>

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:48.620
Mom, could you try sitting 
up for a little bit?

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.330
My body feels so heavy.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.530
<i>There it is!</i>

00:04:58.720 --> 00:04:59.850
What are you doing?

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:01.320
Just hold still.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:04.680
Huh?

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.070
How do you feel now?

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:10.220
Better. My body suddenly feels lighter, too.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.630
The headache and nausea are gone.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.830
<b>Ashiya Nara-sama</b>

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:22.490
I'm surprised.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.170
Remember how I told you I used 
to get anemic all the time?

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:27.130
Yeah.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:31.660
Taking medicine and going to the 
hospital never made it better,

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:35.470
but no matter how bad I felt,

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:39.150
I would always instantly feel better 
when Sakae-kun came around.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:44.110
After he secretly did something 
like you did just now.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:48.030
You take after your dad in a strange way.

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:54.360
Are you a relative of Ashiya-san?

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:56.630
No.

00:05:57.810 --> 00:05:59.040
Excuse me.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:03.500
Ashiya-san, how are you feeling?

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:08.510
I'm feeling much better 
now that my son is here.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:10.680
You must be Hanae-kun.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.520
I'm Hinohara. I called you earlier.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:16.020
Oh, right. Thank you for everything.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:20.650
Is the blond boy outside 
your room your friend?

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:22.550
Blond?

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.430
Abeno-san?

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:31.990
I came to collect the 
hairball, since he escaped.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:39.370
What's this yokai stuck to the hairball?

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:42.490
It was haunting my mom until a minute ago.

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:44.790
She's been feeling better since I removed it.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:47.380
Oh?

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:52.810
I knew I was sitting on something fuzzy.

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:55.550
Was I moving in my sleep?

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:59.140
I must return to that human.

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:02.520
Wait.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:08.100
I apologize for stopping you, but 
could I have a moment of your time?

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.780
I'm Abeno, master of the Mononokean.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.780
The Mononokean...

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:21.610
I decided to haunt that human on a whim!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:28.120
I was simply resting because I happened 
to spot a human vulnerable to haunting

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:30.350
while I was exhausted.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:34.790
I knew it would weaken the 
human, but I had no choice!

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:39.430
I wasn't trying to hurt a human!

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:45.980
So please don't exorcise me!

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:51.130
I don't want to be exorcised to that hell!

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:55.620
Get away from him before he crushes us!

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:03.370
I see. So the Underworld 
isn't a yokai graveyard.

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:06.380
I'm glad you understand.

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:11.880
Aranaki-dono, I could exorcise you 
immediately. Would you like me to?

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:17.100
I'd exhaust myself if I moved 
even a little with this body.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:20.880
It should go back to normal 
if I rest a while, so...

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:23.390
Could you do something for me?

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.190
What's that?

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:29.600
May I haunt that human again?

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:34.700
I was so comfortable.
I was able to sleep soundly.

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:36.740
Is that a no?

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.330
Would you accept a substitute?

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:47.360
This is superbly comfortable, as well.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.460
I can feel the energy rising within me.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.100
Seems like you're a good match for him.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:56.970
I suddenly feel weaker...

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.760
You're like a yokai trap.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:03.560
This weakness feels different 
than when Fuzzy haunted me.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:05.790
I'll be careful not to take too much.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:09.000
"Take"? What is he taking from me?!

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:12.500
Shut up. If you have the 
energy to talk, you're fine.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:17.210
Aranaki-dono, I'll come for you in two hours.

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:19.740
You're welcome to rest until then.

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:24.800
Oh, right. You have work 
to do in the Underworld.

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:27.440
Yeah. I need to get going.

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:29.640
Let's go, hairball. We've got work.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.250
Hanae, it's an emergency!

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.590
What's wrong?

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:43.720
My name's Abeno. Pleased to meet you.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:47.370
Nice to meet you. I'm Hanae's mother.

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:49.730
Sorry I'm not dressed properly.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:53.720
The Monono—I mean, Abeno-san 
brought me to the hospital.

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:56.910
Oh, I'm sorry for the inconvenience 
my son caused you.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:59.150
Did you come by bus?
I can cover his bus fare.

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:01.240
Oh, I don't have my wallet!

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:03.340
Don't worry about it.

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:05.620
Anyway, wasn't there something 
you wanted to say?

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:10.840
Oh, that's right. I left the house 
unlocked when I came here.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.750
I left the shop open, too.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:15.010
Got it. I'll head back there.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:17.010
Thanks.

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:30.520
<i>Golden hair and eyes...</i>

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:32.300
<i>They're the same color.</i>

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:35.380
<i>Just like Sakae-kun.</i>

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.690
<i>A boy like a sunflower.</i>

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:49.350
It's unlocked.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:54.360
I'm home, Hanae.

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:03.180
Ashiya-dono, this is the last one.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.470
Keep it up! Keep it up!

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:06.350
Yeah...

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:12.060
Almost there, almost there...

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.650
Temporarily Closed
 We're terribly sorry, but the 
store will be closed today.
 Manager

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.300
There. All closed up.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:22.480
Good work.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:26.160
Good... work...

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:28.060
I'm exhausted.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:30.830
Did I take too much?

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.790
Hanae!

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:38.340
You can't die!

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:43.640
It's no use. I'll have to...

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:49.640
Look again! I'm alive, Sis!

00:11:57.030 --> 00:12:00.480
Right after I finally came back home, 
I heard Mom was in the hospital.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:04.320
Then I saw you on the ground. 
I was so surprised.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:07.340
Next time you see someone on the ground,

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:09.920
check if they're conscious or 
breathing before you do CPR.

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.790
I thought I'd actually die.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:13.980
I thought I did.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.330
You didn't.

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:21.840
Do you like the omelet rice I made?

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:26.800
It's good, so why don't you 
stop watching me and eat?

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:30.710
That looks good. Could I have a bite?

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:37.630
Sis, could you get the ketchup?

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:38.780
You need more?

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.200
Yeah, just a little.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:41.110
Okay.

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:42.870
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:49.380
It's delicious! I'm in heaven!

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:53.870
My body's back to normal, Ashiya-dono!

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:56.350
<i>Nice work, omelet rice!</i>

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:57.540
<i>Nice work, Sis!</i>

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:02.570
<i>She didn't respond when Aranaki-san 
spoke right in front of her.</i>

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:06.340
<i>She can't see yokai, either.</i>

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:08.380
<i>Neither can Mom.</i>

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:15.020
<i>You take after your dad in a strange way.</i>

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.720
Are you Santa?

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:24.390
No.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:31.870
Santa asked me to come see you.

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:37.170
Then... are you my dad?

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:40.670
Yes.

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:44.250
Nice to meet you, Ashiya Hanae-kun.

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:51.810
Hanae, that's too much ketchup.

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:55.680
Listen, I know this is a weird question...

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.990
Was there anything unusual about Dad?

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:02.190
Like what?

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:05.690
For example, could he see yokai?

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:12.540
Or did you ever see him acting strange?

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:16.000
For example, when mom collapsed 
from anemia like she did today,

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.960
did he ever brush her with his hand, or—

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:18.960
Hanae.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:23.660
I don't want to talk about a 
man who abandoned his family.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:25.590
Don't make me remember him.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:31.510
Sorry.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.580
Sorry about that.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:03.130
You didn't know him, so you need 
me to tell you what he was like.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:11.560
I don't remember him saying 
he could see yokai.

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:15.930
In the first place, do you 
actually believe in yokai?

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:21.260
Did you watch some paranormal 
show over summer break?

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:24.940
You're so impressionable. It's because 
you're such a scaredy-cat.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.960
Yeah...

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:28.560
I'm right here.

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:29.500
But...

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:33.230
Now that you mention it, it was strange

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:38.950
how mom would always get better if he went 
near her when she wasn't feeling well.

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:43.850
On those days, he'd look around a lot

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:46.910
and secretly talk or nod to himself.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:49.970
I remember it because it was so strange.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:55.770
That's all I can remember.

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:08.480
Thanks for telling me.

00:16:13.310 --> 00:16:15.450
I'll go to the hospital with you tomorrow.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.740
Mom will be surprised.

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:25.940
What was that?

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:29.720
Ah, it's you, Fuzzball-dono.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:32.170
You came to get me.

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:35.520
Ashiya-dono, let's head to the Mononokean.

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:38.810
I should be getting exorcised soon.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:41.480
What are you smiling and nodding about?

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:44.060
Sis, I'm going out for a bit.

00:16:44.430 --> 00:16:45.820
At this hour?

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:48.060
I'll be right back.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.110
Wait...

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:03.030
If you don't come back, like he 
never did, I'll never forgive you.

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:08.170
Abeno-san, it's an emergency!

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:12.170
Huh? He's not here?

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.000
Mononokean, where's Abeno-san?

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:24.350
Master of the Mononokean, Abeno Haruitsuki,

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:27.350
requesting a portal to the Underworld.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.460
Thank you for everything.

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:45.120
Ashiya-dono, I'll never 
forget that wonderful meal.

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:48.120
It was just plain old omelet rice.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:51.450
You and your family take care.

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:53.290
We will.

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:02.140
<i>Family, huh?</i>

00:18:02.550 --> 00:18:05.390
So, what's the emergency?

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:10.970
Is your mother being 
haunted by another yokai?

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:16.070
No... It doesn't matter at all to you,

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:20.070
but my dad could apparently see yokai.

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:25.080
My dad's actually been missing for years.

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:30.540
I have no way of confirming it, 
so I could be making it up,

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:33.590
but based on what I've heard about his 
behavior, I'm pretty sure he could.

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:34.970
What behavior?

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.920
Looking around, talking to himself...

00:18:38.920 --> 00:18:41.500
Things I can remember myself doing.

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:46.490
If he could see yokai, he may have 
known about the Mononokean.

00:18:47.240 --> 00:18:51.900
Abeno-san, do you recognize 
the name Ashiya Sakae?

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:53.080
I do.

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:56.990
What?

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.040
You do?!

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:59.990
Since when? Why? How?!

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:03.530
Today! At the hospital! I heard his name!

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.540
Where is he?

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:14.250
It's not a happy story. 
Do you still want to hear it?

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:18.260
Please tell me.

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:22.520
A while back, the previous 
master of the Mononokean

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:25.260
mentioned the name Ashiya Sakae.

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:27.350
Aoi-san did?

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:32.340
According to Aoi, Ashiya 
Sakae died a long time ago.

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:33.900
What?

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:36.910
I don't know exactly when,

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:41.610
but if I recall the story correctly, 
it was about 100 years ago.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:44.760
100 years? Wait...

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:47.690
My parents traveled across 
space-time to meet?

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:49.610
Like the boy and girl who leapt through time?

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:51.870
That's why I didn't make the connection.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:54.540
Maybe they just share the same name?

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:59.550
No. I know what I said, but it's likely 
the number of years is ambiguous.

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:03.180
A yokai's sense of time is way off.

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:09.180
Come to think of it, Yahiko said you 
two played together 30 years ago.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:12.010
It was actually nine years.

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:17.030
And there aren't many 
humans who can see yokai.

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:21.030
They're almost definitely the same person.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.160
Was it illness? An accident?

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.030
Or was there some other cause?

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:33.040
If he was a client of the Mononokean, 
it would've been recorded in the log.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.510
<i>He's dead.</i>

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:42.050
The first time my dad disappeared 
was just before I was born.

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:46.860
It was sudden, so they thought he got 
in an accident or involved in a crime.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:50.810
My mom and sister were really worried.

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:54.810
But three years later on Christmas...

00:20:57.570 --> 00:20:59.820
Dad!

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:04.310
He was gone the next morning.

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:07.240
He hasn't been back since.

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:12.710
I never saw my dad before or after that.

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:14.550
That was the only time.

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:18.640
If you're right and he's already dead,

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:21.370
then something must've happened 
to him after that day.

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:22.860
Well?

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:23.720
Huh?

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:25.210
What do you want to do?

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:27.720
If you want, I'll look into it.

00:21:32.660 --> 00:21:36.230
I don't want to talk about a 
man who abandoned his family.

00:21:43.310 --> 00:21:45.450
Hanae's late.

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:47.390
Maybe I'll call him.

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:51.380
My family's just the three of us.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:53.930
I see.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Time: "The Messenger"</b>

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:27.580
Cultural festival? What?

00:23:27.580 --> 00:23:29.880
Cosplay? Why me?

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:32.390
Hey, Yahiko. Quit fooling 
around at the school.

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:35.180
Fine. Do whatever you want.

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:37.100
Next time, "The Messenger."

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:38.640
Trick-or-treat.
